[{"id":"taba-5-39-1","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajao se","en":"he/it repented"},{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"},{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"pokajao sam se","en":"I repented"}],"ref":"5:39","answerWord":"تَابَ","answerSound":"audio/8f03a74fa1e17e8bea04.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But whoso repenteth after his wrongdoing and amendeth, lo! Allah will relent toward him. Lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["فَمَن","تَابَ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِ","ظُلْمِهِۦ","وَأَصْلَحَ","فَإِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يَتُوبُ","عَلَيْهِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-2-160-2","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajali su se","en":"they repented"},{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"},{"bs":"kaje se","en":"he/it repents"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"}],"ref":"2:160","answerWord":"تَابُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/17bbf52eeb8a2471fa8e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Except those who repent and amend and make manifest (the truth). These it is toward whom I relent. I am the Relenting, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["إِلَّا","ٱلَّذِينَ","تَابُوا۟","وَأَصْلَحُوا۟","وَبَيَّنُوا۟","فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","أَتُوبُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","وَأَنَا","ٱلتَّوَّابُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-20-122-3","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"},{"bs":"pokajao sam se","en":"I repented"},{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"}],"ref":"20:122","answerWord":"فَتَابَ","answerSound":"audio/621b9cfa7d232bcfe91f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then his Lord chose him, and relented toward him, and guided him.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["ثُمَّ","ٱجْتَبَٰهُ","رَبُّهُۥ","فَتَابَ","عَلَيْهِ","وَهَدَىٰ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-4-17-13","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"},{"bs":"i primio je pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepted repentance"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"}],"ref":"4:17","answerWord":"يَتُوبُ","answerSound":"audio/b29922de8c94d5d9f194.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Forgiveness is only incumbent on Allah toward those who do evil in ignorance (and) then turn quickly (in repentance) to Allah. These are they toward whom Allah relenteth. Allah is ever Knower, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["إِنَّمَا","ٱلتَّوْبَةُ","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","لِلَّذِينَ","يَعْمَلُونَ","ٱلسُّوٓءَ","بِجَهَٰلَةٍ","ثُمَّ","يَتُوبُونَ","مِن","قَرِيبٍ","فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","يَتُوبُ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","وَكَانَ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلِيمًا","حَكِيمًا"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-11-90-3","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"},{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"i primio je pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepted repentance"}],"ref":"11:90","answerWord":"تُوبُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/20e6dbf5be3e5c01f755.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Ask pardon of your Lord and then turn unto Him (repentant). Lo! my Lord is Merciful, Loving.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["وَٱسْتَغْفِرُوا۟","رَبَّكُمْ","ثُمَّ","تُوبُوٓا۟","إِلَيْهِ","إِنَّ","رَبِّى","رَحِيمٌ","وَدُودٌ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-3-128-6","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"pokajao sam se","en":"I repented"},{"bs":"pokajali su se","en":"they repented"},{"bs":"primio je pokajanje","en":"he/it accepted repentance"}],"ref":"3:128","answerWord":"يَتُوبَ","answerSound":"audio/b30587dcc4479cd75d41.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"It is no concern at all of thee (Muhammad) whether He relent toward them or punish them; for they are evil-doers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["لَيْسَ","لَكَ","مِنَ","ٱلْأَمْرِ","شَىْءٌ","أَوْ","يَتُوبَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","أَوْ","يُعَذِّبَهُمْ","فَإِنَّهُمْ","ظَٰلِمُونَ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-5-74-1","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"(zar se neće) pokajati","en":"(will they not) repent"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"},{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"}],"ref":"5:74","answerWord":"يَتُوبُونَ","answerSound":"audio/8103846da2dfb4b495a1.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Will they not rather turn unto Allah and seek forgiveness of Him? For Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["أَفَلَا","يَتُوبُونَ","إِلَى","ٱللَّهِ","وَيَسْتَغْفِرُونَهُۥ","وَٱللَّهُ","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-4-18-12","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajao sam se","en":"I repented"},{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"(zar se neće) pokajati","en":"(will they not) repent"},{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"}],"ref":"4:18","answerWord":"تُبْتُ","answerSound":"audio/df9b2d58d2ce677d3943.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The forgiveness is not for those who do ill-deeds until, when death attendeth upon one of them, he saith: Lo! I repent now; nor yet for those who die while they are disbelievers. For such We have prepared a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["وَلَيْسَتِ","ٱلتَّوْبَةُ","لِلَّذِينَ","يَعْمَلُونَ","ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ","حَتَّىٰٓ","إِذَا","حَضَرَ","أَحَدَهُمُ","ٱلْمَوْتُ","قَالَ","إِنِّى","تُبْتُ","ٱلْـَٰٔنَ","وَلَا","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَمُوتُونَ","وَهُمْ","كُفَّارٌ","أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","أَعْتَدْنَا","لَهُمْ","عَذَابًا","أَلِيمًا"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-2-279-9","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajali ste se","en":"you (all) repented"},{"bs":"pokajao sam se","en":"I repented"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"}],"ref":"2:279","answerWord":"تُبْتُمْ","answerSound":"audio/796e4ead114fc7b709b7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if ye do not, then be warned of war (against you) from Allah and His messenger. And if ye repent, then ye have your principal (without interest). Wrong not, and ye shall not be wronged.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["فَإِن","لَّمْ","تَفْعَلُوا۟","فَأْذَنُوا۟","بِحَرْبٍ","مِّنَ","ٱللَّهِ","وَرَسُولِهِۦ","وَإِن","تُبْتُمْ","فَلَكُمْ","رُءُوسُ","أَمْوَٰلِكُمْ","لَا","تَظْلِمُونَ","وَلَا","تُظْلَمُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-4-26-9","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"(zar se neće) pokajati","en":"(will they not) repent"},{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"}],"ref":"4:26","answerWord":"وَيَتُوبَ","answerSound":"audio/50b8179c8ecde2c5867e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah would explain to you and guide you by the examples of those who were before you, and would turn to you in mercy. Allah is Knower, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["يُرِيدُ","ٱللَّهُ","لِيُبَيِّنَ","لَكُمْ","وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ","سُنَنَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","مِن","قَبْلِكُمْ","وَيَتُوبَ","عَلَيْكُمْ","وَٱللَّهُ","عَلِيمٌ","حَكِيمٌ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-2-128-11","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"},{"bs":"i primio je pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepted repentance"},{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"(zar se neće) pokajati","en":"(will they not) repent"}],"ref":"2:128","answerWord":"وَتُبْ","answerSound":"audio/1082ea5cf43eb70c1884.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Our Lord! And make us submissive unto Thee and of our seed a nation submissive unto Thee, and show us our ways of worship, and relent toward us. Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Relenting, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["رَبَّنَا","وَٱجْعَلْنَا","مُسْلِمَيْنِ","لَكَ","وَمِن","ذُرِّيَّتِنَآ","أُمَّةً","مُّسْلِمَةً","لَّكَ","وَأَرِنَا","مَنَاسِكَنَا","وَتُبْ","عَلَيْنَآ","إِنَّكَ","أَنتَ","ٱلتَّوَّابُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-2-160-6","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"pa mu je primio pokajanje","en":"so He accepted (his) repentance"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"},{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"}],"ref":"2:160","answerWord":"أَتُوبُ","answerSound":"audio/23156cec7ef62da609c2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Except those who repent and amend and make manifest (the truth). These it is toward whom I relent. I am the Relenting, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["إِلَّا","ٱلَّذِينَ","تَابُوا۟","وَأَصْلَحُوا۟","وَبَيَّنُوا۟","فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","أَتُوبُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","وَأَنَا","ٱلتَّوَّابُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-4-16-5","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"pokajali su se","en":"they (two) repented"},{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"},{"bs":"da se kaju","en":"so that they may repent"},{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"}],"ref":"4:16","answerWord":"تَابَا","answerSound":"audio/82ca2f5e612d5a28c1ea.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And as for the two of you who are guilty thereof, punish them both. And if they repent and improve, then let them be. Lo! Allah is ever relenting, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["وَٱلَّذَانِ","يَأْتِيَٰنِهَا","مِنكُمْ","فَـَٔاذُوهُمَا","فَإِن","تَابَا","وَأَصْلَحَا","فَأَعْرِضُوا۟","عَنْهُمَآ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","كَانَ","تَوَّابًا","رَّحِيمًا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-9-15-3","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"i prima pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"pokajao se","en":"he/it repented"},{"bs":"pokajali su se","en":"they repented"},{"bs":"(zar se neće) pokajati","en":"(will they not) repent"}],"ref":"9:15","answerWord":"وَيَتُوبُ","answerSound":"audio/443c85fa1e24b4f5fb60.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And He will remove the anger of their hearts. Allah relenteth toward whom He will. Allah is Knower, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["وَيُذْهِبْ","غَيْظَ","قُلُوبِهِمْ","وَيَتُوبُ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَىٰ","مَن","يَشَآءُ","وَٱللَّهُ","عَلِيمٌ","حَكِيمٌ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-9-117-1","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"primio je pokajanje","en":"he/it accepted repentance"},{"bs":"kaje se","en":"he/it repents"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"i primi pokajanje!","en":"and accept repentance!"}],"ref":"9:117","answerWord":"تَّابَ","answerSound":"audio/e82c9097e4129e75c751.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah hath turned in mercy to the Prophet, and to the Muhajirin and the Ansar who followed him in the hour of hardship. After the hearts of a party of them had almost swerved aside, then turned He unto them in mercy. Lo! He is Full of Pity, Merciful for them.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["لَّقَد","تَّابَ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَى","ٱلنَّبِىِّ","وَٱلْمُهَٰجِرِينَ","وَٱلْأَنصَارِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱتَّبَعُوهُ","فِى","سَاعَةِ","ٱلْعُسْرَةِ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِ","مَا","كَادَ","يَزِيغُ","قُلُوبُ","فَرِيقٍ","مِّنْهُمْ","ثُمَّ","تَابَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","إِنَّهُۥ","بِهِمْ","رَءُوفٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"taba-58-13-10","words":["verb:taba"],"options":[{"bs":"i primio je pokajanje","en":"and he/it accepted repentance"},{"bs":"prima pokajanje","en":"he/it accepts repentance"},{"bs":"primam pokajanje","en":"I accept repentance"},{"bs":"pokajte se!","en":"repent!"}],"ref":"58:13","answerWord":"وَتَابَ","answerSound":"audio/a78beef09d0b6bccfcc5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Fear ye to offer alms before your conference? Then, when ye do it not and Allah hath forgiven you, establish worship and pay the poor-due and obey Allah and His messenger. And Allah is Aware of what ye do.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pokajati se","en":"to repent, to turn in repentance"},"passage":["ءَأَشْفَقْتُمْ","أَن","تُقَدِّمُوا۟","بَيْنَ","يَدَىْ","نَجْوَىٰكُمْ","صَدَقَٰتٍ","فَإِذْ","لَمْ","تَفْعَلُوا۟","وَتَابَ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَيْكُمْ","فَأَقِيمُوا۟","ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ","وَءَاتُوا۟","ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ","وَأَطِيعُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","وَرَسُولَهُۥ","وَٱللَّهُ","خَبِيرٌۢ","بِمَا","تَعْمَلُونَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"تابَ"}},{"id":"dalla-37-71-1","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"zalutala je","en":"went astray"},{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"},{"bs":"pa su zalutali","en":"so they went astray"},{"bs":"lutaju","en":"they go astray"}],"ref":"37:71","answerWord":"ضَلَّ","answerSound":"audio/c63d0d9b111cc461275e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And verily most of the men of old went astray before them,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["وَلَقَدْ","ضَلَّ","قَبْلَهُمْ","أَكْثَرُ","ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-4-167-8","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"},{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"},{"bs":"zalutala je","en":"went astray"}],"ref":"4:167","answerWord":"ضَلُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/df50705a7d3289a10cd2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! those who disbelieve and hinder (others) from the way of Allah, they verily have wandered far astray.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","وَصَدُّوا۟","عَن","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","قَدْ","ضَلُّوا۟","ضَلَٰلًۢا","بَعِيدًا"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-6-24-5","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"i nestao je","en":"and he/it was lost"},{"bs":"zalutao sam","en":"I went astray"},{"bs":"i zalutali su","en":"and they went astray"},{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"}],"ref":"6:24","answerWord":"وَضَلَّ","answerSound":"audio/4942a8962688a0f63c61.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"See how they lie against themselves, and (how) the thing which they devised hath failed them!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["ٱنظُرْ","كَيْفَ","كَذَبُوا۟","عَلَىٰٓ","أَنفُسِهِمْ","وَضَلَّ","عَنْهُم","مَّا","كَانُوا۟","يَفْتَرُونَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-6-117-5","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"},{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"},{"bs":"zalutao sam","en":"I went astray"},{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"}],"ref":"6:117","answerWord":"يَضِلُّ","answerSound":"audio/50d120b0a8e56258a031.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! thy Lord, He knoweth best who erreth from His way; and He knoweth best (who are) the rightly guided.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["إِنَّ","رَبَّكَ","هُوَ","أَعْلَمُ","مَن","يَضِلُّ","عَن","سَبِيلِهِۦ","وَهُوَ","أَعْلَمُ","بِٱلْمُهْتَدِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-4-44-12","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"lutate","en":"you (all) go astray"},{"bs":"lutaju","en":"they go astray"},{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"}],"ref":"4:44","answerWord":"تَضِلُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/d375b5d46bd17b13bb93.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Seest thou not those unto whom a portion of the Scripture hath been given, how they purchase error, and seek to make you (Muslims) err from the right way?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["أَلَمْ","تَرَ","إِلَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","أُوتُوا۟","نَصِيبًا","مِّنَ","ٱلْكِتَٰبِ","يَشْتَرُونَ","ٱلضَّلَٰلَةَ","وَيُرِيدُونَ","أَن","تَضِلُّوا۟","ٱلسَّبِيلَ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-6-56-15","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"zalutao sam","en":"I went astray"},{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"},{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"},{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"}],"ref":"6:56","answerWord":"ضَلَلْتُ","answerSound":"audio/04e968afdb1ebbda76b9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: I am forbidden to worship those on whom ye call instead of Allah. Say: I will not follow your desires, for then should I go astray and I should not be of the rightly guided.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["قُلْ","إِنِّى","نُهِيتُ","أَنْ","أَعْبُدَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","تَدْعُونَ","مِن","دُونِ","ٱللَّهِ","قُل","لَّآ","أَتَّبِعُ","أَهْوَآءَكُمْ","قَدْ","ضَلَلْتُ","إِذًا","وَمَآ","أَنَا۠","مِنَ","ٱلْمُهْتَدِينَ"],"marked":[15],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-17-48-5","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"pa su zalutali","en":"so they went astray"},{"bs":"lutate","en":"you (all) go astray"},{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"}],"ref":"17:48","answerWord":"فَضَلُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/adc030adbb360aff993e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"See what similitudes they coin for thee, and thus are all astray, and cannot find a road!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["ٱنظُرْ","كَيْفَ","ضَرَبُوا۟","لَكَ","ٱلْأَمْثَالَ","فَضَلُّوا۟","فَلَا","يَسْتَطِيعُونَ","سَبِيلًا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-5-77-19","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"i zalutali su","en":"and they went astray"},{"bs":"zalutala je","en":"went astray"},{"bs":"lutate","en":"you (all) go astray"},{"bs":"zalutao sam","en":"I went astray"}],"ref":"5:77","answerWord":"وَضَلُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/40038cc517c3d5c7edd9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: O People of the Scripture! Stress not in your religion other than the truth, and follow not the vain desires of folk who erred of old and led many astray, and erred from a plain road.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["قُلْ","يَٰٓأَهْلَ","ٱلْكِتَٰبِ","لَا","تَغْلُوا۟","فِى","دِينِكُمْ","غَيْرَ","ٱلْحَقِّ","وَلَا","تَتَّبِعُوٓا۟","أَهْوَآءَ","قَوْمٍ","قَدْ","ضَلُّوا۟","مِن","قَبْلُ","وَأَضَلُّوا۟","كَثِيرًا","وَضَلُّوا۟","عَن","سَوَآءِ","ٱلسَّبِيلِ"],"marked":[19],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-20-92-6","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"},{"bs":"zalutala je","en":"went astray"},{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"}],"ref":"20:92","answerWord":"ضَلُّوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/e75a1124e41050d0a825.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He (Moses) said: O Aaron! What held thee back when thou didst see them gone astray,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["قَالَ","يَٰهَٰرُونُ","مَا","مَنَعَكَ","إِذْ","رَأَيْتَهُمْ","ضَلُّوٓا۟"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-32-10-2","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"},{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"},{"bs":"lutate","en":"you (all) go astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"}],"ref":"32:10","answerWord":"ضَلَلْنَا","answerSound":"audio/e9af33b07d0160045f98.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they say: When we are lost in the earth, how can we then be re-created? Nay but they are disbelievers in the meeting with their Lord.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["وَقَالُوٓا۟","أَءِذَا","ضَلَلْنَا","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","أَءِنَّا","لَفِى","خَلْقٍ","جَدِيدٍۭ","بَلْ","هُم","بِلِقَآءِ","رَبِّهِمْ","كَٰفِرُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-34-50-4","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"lutam","en":"I go astray"},{"bs":"lutate","en":"you (all) go astray"},{"bs":"zalutala je","en":"went astray"},{"bs":"zalutao sam","en":"I went astray"}],"ref":"34:50","answerWord":"أَضِلُّ","answerSound":"audio/c451e77bf4cb0326dec4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: If I err, I err only to my own loss, and if I am rightly guided it is because of that which my Lord hath revealed unto me. Lo! He is Hearer, Nigh.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["قُلْ","إِن","ضَلَلْتُ","فَإِنَّمَآ","أَضِلُّ","عَلَىٰ","نَفْسِى","وَإِنِ","ٱهْتَدَيْتُ","فَبِمَا","يُوحِىٓ","إِلَىَّ","رَبِّىٓ","إِنَّهُۥ","سَمِيعٌ","قَرِيبٌ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"dalla-38-26-19","words":["verb:dalla"],"options":[{"bs":"lutaju","en":"they go astray"},{"bs":"zaluta","en":"goes astray"},{"bs":"izgubili smo se","en":"we were lost"},{"bs":"zalutali su","en":"they went astray"}],"ref":"38:26","answerWord":"يَضِلُّونَ","answerSound":"audio/d215eac793b65b934d95.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(And it was said unto him): O David! Lo! We have set thee as a viceroy in the earth; therefor judge aright between mankind, and follow not desire that it beguile thee from the way of Allah. Lo! those who wander from the way of Allah have an awful doom, forasmuch as they forgot the Day of Reckoning.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"zalutati","en":"to go astray"},"passage":["يَٰدَاوُۥدُ","إِنَّا","جَعَلْنَٰكَ","خَلِيفَةً","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","فَٱحْكُم","بَيْنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","بِٱلْحَقِّ","وَلَا","تَتَّبِعِ","ٱلْهَوَىٰ","فَيُضِلَّكَ","عَن","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَضِلُّونَ","عَن","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","لَهُمْ","عَذَابٌ","شَدِيدٌۢ","بِمَا","نَسُوا۟","يَوْمَ","ٱلْحِسَابِ"],"marked":[19],"facts":{"verb":"ضَلَّ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-26-217-0","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"i osloni se!","en":"and rely!"},{"bs":"oslonite se!","en":"(you all) rely!"},{"bs":"oslanja se","en":"he/it relies"},{"bs":"oslonio sam se","en":"I relied"}],"ref":"26:217","answerWord":"وَتَوَكَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/77afa6b778054b58abe4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And put thy trust in the Mighty, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["وَتَوَكَّلْ","عَلَى","ٱلْعَزِيزِ","ٱلرَّحِيمِ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-9-129-10","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"oslonio sam se","en":"I relied"},{"bs":"i osloni se!","en":"and rely!"},{"bs":"oslanja se","en":"he/it relies"},{"bs":"oslonili smo se","en":"we relied"}],"ref":"9:129","answerWord":"تَوَكَّلْتُ","answerSound":"audio/ae9b848460e1fac96975.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Now, if they turn away (O Muhammad) say: Allah sufficeth me. There is no Allah save Him. In Him have I put my trust, and He is Lord of the Tremendous Throne.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["فَإِن","تَوَلَّوْا۟","فَقُلْ","حَسْبِىَ","ٱللَّهُ","لَآ","إِلَٰهَ","إِلَّا","هُوَ","عَلَيْهِ","تَوَكَّلْتُ","وَهُوَ","رَبُّ","ٱلْعَرْشِ","ٱلْعَظِيمِ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-16-42-4","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"oslanjaju se","en":"they rely"},{"bs":"oslanja se","en":"he/it relies"},{"bs":"i osloni se!","en":"and rely!"},{"bs":"oslanjamo se","en":"we rely"}],"ref":"16:42","answerWord":"يَتَوَكَّلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/e9eb227e7bd5056bcbef.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Such as are steadfast and put their trust in Allah.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["ٱلَّذِينَ","صَبَرُوا۟","وَعَلَىٰ","رَبِّهِمْ","يَتَوَكَّلُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-10-85-3","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"oslonili smo se","en":"we relied"},{"bs":"pa se osloni!","en":"so rely!"},{"bs":"oslanjaju se","en":"they rely"},{"bs":"oslanjamo se","en":"we rely"}],"ref":"10:85","answerWord":"تَوَكَّلْنَا","answerSound":"audio/1b09761146bed7a58940.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They said: In Allah we put trust. Our Lord! Oh, make us not a lure for the wrongdoing folk;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["فَقَالُوا۟","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","تَوَكَّلْنَا","رَبَّنَا","لَا","تَجْعَلْنَا","فِتْنَةً","لِّلْقَوْمِ","ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-3-159-23","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa se osloni!","en":"so rely!"},{"bs":"oslonio sam se","en":"I relied"},{"bs":"oslanjamo se","en":"we rely"},{"bs":"oslanjaju se","en":"they rely"}],"ref":"3:159","answerWord":"فَتَوَكَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/847fc5e8425d951c6d04.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"It was by the mercy of Allah that thou wast lenient with them (O Muhammad), for if thou hadst been stern and fierce of heart they would have dispersed from round about thee. So pardon them and ask forgiveness for them and consult with them upon the conduct of affairs. And when thou art resolved, then put thy trust in Allah. Lo! Allah loveth those who put their trust (in Him).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["فَبِمَا","رَحْمَةٍ","مِّنَ","ٱللَّهِ","لِنتَ","لَهُمْ","وَلَوْ","كُنتَ","فَظًّا","غَلِيظَ","ٱلْقَلْبِ","لَٱنفَضُّوا۟","مِنْ","حَوْلِكَ","فَٱعْفُ","عَنْهُمْ","وَٱسْتَغْفِرْ","لَهُمْ","وَشَاوِرْهُمْ","فِى","ٱلْأَمْرِ","فَإِذَا","عَزَمْتَ","فَتَوَكَّلْ","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يُحِبُّ","ٱلْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ"],"marked":[23],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-8-49-11","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"oslanja se","en":"he/it relies"},{"bs":"oslonio sam se","en":"I relied"},{"bs":"oslonili smo se","en":"we relied"},{"bs":"oslanjamo se","en":"we rely"}],"ref":"8:49","answerWord":"يَتَوَكَّلْ","answerSound":"audio/31c8676857c8467c757e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"When the hypocrites and those in whose hearts is a disease said: Their religion hath deluded these. Whoso putteth his trust in Allah (will find that) lo! Allah is Mighty, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["إِذْ","يَقُولُ","ٱلْمُنَٰفِقُونَ","وَٱلَّذِينَ","فِى","قُلُوبِهِم","مَّرَضٌ","غَرَّ","هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ","دِينُهُمْ","وَمَن","يَتَوَكَّلْ","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","فَإِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","عَزِيزٌ","حَكِيمٌ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"tawakkala-14-12-3","words":["verb:tawakkala"],"options":[{"bs":"oslanjamo se","en":"we rely"},{"bs":"i osloni se!","en":"and rely!"},{"bs":"oslonite se!","en":"(you all) rely!"},{"bs":"oslonio sam se","en":"I relied"}],"ref":"14:12","answerWord":"نَتَوَكَّلَ","answerSound":"audio/6b1217e751abb74e6a6a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"How should we not put our trust in Allah when He hath shown us our ways? We surely will endure the hurt ye do us. In Allah let the trusting put their trust.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"osloniti se, pouzdati se","en":"to rely, to trust"},"passage":["وَمَا","لَنَآ","أَلَّا","نَتَوَكَّلَ","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","وَقَدْ","هَدَىٰنَا","سُبُلَنَا","وَلَنَصْبِرَنَّ","عَلَىٰ","مَآ","ءَاذَيْتُمُونَا","وَعَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ","ٱلْمُتَوَكِّلُونَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"تَوَكَّلَ"}},{"id":"fataha-48-1-1","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"otvorili smo","en":"We have opened"},{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"},{"bs":"presudi!","en":"judge!"},{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"}],"ref":"48:1","answerWord":"فَتَحْنَا","answerSound":"audio/9a10ce845cc13d6f50b9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! We have given thee (O Muhammad) a signal victory,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["إِنَّا","فَتَحْنَا","لَكَ","فَتْحًا","مُّبِينًا"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-21-96-2","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"otvoreno je","en":"it was opened"},{"bs":"otvorili smo","en":"We have opened"},{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"},{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"}],"ref":"21:96","answerWord":"فُتِحَتْ","answerSound":"audio/6a25a1f67572611c53f7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Until, when Gog and Magog are let loose, and they hasten out of every mound,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["حَتَّىٰٓ","إِذَا","فُتِحَتْ","يَأْجُوجُ","وَمَأْجُوجُ","وَهُم","مِّن","كُلِّ","حَدَبٍ","يَنسِلُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-2-76-14","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"otvorio je","en":"he/it opened"},{"bs":"otvorili smo","en":"We have opened"},{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"},{"bs":"i otvoreno je","en":"and it was opened"}],"ref":"2:76","answerWord":"فَتَحَ","answerSound":"audio/006968f982a437bd32bb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when they fall in with those who believe, they say: We believe. But when they go apart one with another they say: Prate ye to them of that which Allah hath disclosed to you that they may contend with you before your Lord concerning it? Have ye then no sense?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["وَإِذَا","لَقُوا۟","ٱلَّذِينَ","ءَامَنُوا۟","قَالُوٓا۟","ءَامَنَّا","وَإِذَا","خَلَا","بَعْضُهُمْ","إِلَىٰ","بَعْضٍ","قَالُوٓا۟","أَتُحَدِّثُونَهُم","بِمَا","فَتَحَ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَيْكُمْ","لِيُحَآجُّوكُم","بِهِۦ","عِندَ","رَبِّكُمْ","أَفَلَا","تَعْقِلُونَ"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-12-65-1","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"},{"bs":"otvorio je","en":"he/it opened"},{"bs":"otvoreno je","en":"it was opened"},{"bs":"zato presudi","en":"so judge"}],"ref":"12:65","answerWord":"فَتَحُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/f005be0c96934de96456.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when they opened their belongings they discovered that their merchandise had been returned to them. They said: O our father! What (more) can we ask? Here is our merchandise returned to us. We shall get provision for our folk and guard our brother, and we shall have the extra measure of a camel (load). This (that we bring now) is a light measure.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["وَلَمَّا","فَتَحُوا۟","مَتَٰعَهُمْ","وَجَدُوا۟","بِضَٰعَتَهُمْ","رُدَّتْ","إِلَيْهِمْ","قَالُوا۟","يَٰٓأَبَانَا","مَا","نَبْغِى","هَٰذِهِۦ","بِضَٰعَتُنَا","رُدَّتْ","إِلَيْنَا","وَنَمِيرُ","أَهْلَنَا","وَنَحْفَظُ","أَخَانَا","وَنَزْدَادُ","كَيْلَ","بَعِيرٍ","ذَٰلِكَ","كَيْلٌ","يَسِيرٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-26-118-0","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"zato presudi","en":"so judge"},{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"},{"bs":"presudit će","en":"He will judge"},{"bs":"pa smo otvorili","en":"so we opened"}],"ref":"26:118","answerWord":"فَٱفْتَحْ","answerSound":"audio/5a96024595b20e013f88.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Therefor judge Thou between us, a (conclusive) judgment, and save me and those believers who are with me.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["فَٱفْتَحْ","بَيْنِى","وَبَيْنَهُمْ","فَتْحًا","وَنَجِّنِى","وَمَن","مَّعِىَ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-34-26-5","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"presudit će","en":"He will judge"},{"bs":"pa smo otvorili","en":"so we opened"},{"bs":"zato presudi","en":"so judge"},{"bs":"otvoreno je","en":"it was opened"}],"ref":"34:26","answerWord":"يَفْتَحُ","answerSound":"audio/75457bfc8fd93aa14f79.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: Our Lord will bring us all together, then He will judge between us with truth. He is the All-knowing Judge.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["قُلْ","يَجْمَعُ","بَيْنَنَا","رَبُّنَا","ثُمَّ","يَفْتَحُ","بَيْنَنَا","بِٱلْحَقِّ","وَهُوَ","ٱلْفَتَّاحُ","ٱلْعَلِيمُ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-35-2-1","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"},{"bs":"presudi!","en":"judge!"},{"bs":"pa smo otvorili","en":"so we opened"},{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"}],"ref":"35:2","answerWord":"يَفْتَحِ","answerSound":"audio/d752ccbbe230ca014910.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"That which Allah openeth unto mankind of mercy none can withhold it; and that which He withholdeth none can release thereafter. He is the Mighty, the Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["مَّا","يَفْتَحِ","ٱللَّهُ","لِلنَّاسِ","مِن","رَّحْمَةٍ","فَلَا","مُمْسِكَ","لَهَا","وَمَا","يُمْسِكْ","فَلَا","مُرْسِلَ","لَهُۥ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِهِۦ","وَهُوَ","ٱلْعَزِيزُ","ٱلْحَكِيمُ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-39-73-10","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"i otvoreno je","en":"and it was opened"},{"bs":"otvorili smo","en":"We have opened"},{"bs":"otvorili su","en":"they opened"},{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"}],"ref":"39:73","answerWord":"وَفُتِحَتْ","answerSound":"audio/eac69ddaa8460f7f7303.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And those who keep their duty to their Lord are driven unto the Garden in troops till, when they reach it, and the gates thereof are opened, and the warders thereof say unto them: Peace be unto you! Ye are good, so enter ye (the Garden of delight), to dwell therein;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["وَسِيقَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱتَّقَوْا۟","رَبَّهُمْ","إِلَى","ٱلْجَنَّةِ","زُمَرًا","حَتَّىٰٓ","إِذَا","جَآءُوهَا","وَفُتِحَتْ","أَبْوَٰبُهَا","وَقَالَ","لَهُمْ","خَزَنَتُهَا","سَلَٰمٌ","عَلَيْكُمْ","طِبْتُمْ","فَٱدْخُلُوهَا","خَٰلِدِينَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-54-11-0","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"pa smo otvorili","en":"so we opened"},{"bs":"otvoreno je","en":"it was opened"},{"bs":"otvara","en":"he/it opens"},{"bs":"zato presudi","en":"so judge"}],"ref":"54:11","answerWord":"فَفَتَحْنَآ","answerSound":"audio/6a9b460394627336499c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then opened We the gates of heaven with pouring water","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["فَفَتَحْنَآ","أَبْوَٰبَ","ٱلسَّمَآءِ","بِمَآءٍ","مُّنْهَمِرٍ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"fataha-78-19-0","words":["verb:fataha"],"options":[{"bs":"i otvoreno je","en":"and it was opened"},{"bs":"otvorio je","en":"he/it opened"},{"bs":"pa smo otvorili","en":"so we opened"},{"bs":"zato presudi","en":"so judge"}],"ref":"78:19","answerWord":"وَفُتِحَتِ","answerSound":"audio/5494f4e77615026b3884.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And the heaven is opened and becometh as gates,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"otvoriti","en":"to open"},"passage":["وَفُتِحَتِ","ٱلسَّمَآءُ","فَكَانَتْ","أَبْوَٰبًا"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"فَتَحَ"}},{"id":"anqadha-36-23-14","words":["verb:anqadha"],"options":[{"bs":"spašavaju me","en":"they rescue me"},{"bs":"pa vas je spasio","en":"so he/it rescued you (all)"},{"bs":"bivaju spašeni","en":"they are rescued"},{"bs":"spasiš","en":"rescue"}],"ref":"36:23","answerWord":"يُنقِذُونِ","answerSound":"audio/b6aad61cd701d50e071f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Shall I take (other) gods in place of Him when, if the Beneficent should wish me any harm, their intercession will avail me naught, nor can they save?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"spasiti","en":"to rescue, to save"},"passage":["ءَأَتَّخِذُ","مِن","دُونِهِۦٓ","ءَالِهَةً","إِن","يُرِدْنِ","ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ","بِضُرٍّ","لَّا","تُغْنِ","عَنِّى","شَفَٰعَتُهُمْ","شَيْـًٔا","وَلَا","يُنقِذُونِ"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"أَنقَذَ"}},{"id":"anqadha-36-43-8","words":["verb:anqadha"],"options":[{"bs":"bivaju spašeni","en":"they are rescued"},{"bs":"spasiš","en":"rescue"},{"bs":"spašavaju me","en":"they rescue me"},{"bs":"pa vas je spasio","en":"so he/it rescued you (all)"}],"ref":"36:43","answerWord":"يُنقَذُونَ","answerSound":"audio/91eaee818ca463e1de2b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if We will, We drown them, and there is no help for them, neither can they be saved;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"spasiti","en":"to rescue, to save"},"passage":["وَإِن","نَّشَأْ","نُغْرِقْهُمْ","فَلَا","صَرِيخَ","لَهُمْ","وَلَا","هُمْ","يُنقَذُونَ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"أَنقَذَ"}}]